{
    "background_story": "Charli was a brilliant and feisty engineer who had a way with machines. Growing up in a family of tinkerers, she learned to wield a screwdriver before she could ride a bike. As she honed her skills, Charli became known for her ability to fix anything from a leaky faucet to a malfunctioning robot. Her trusty screwdriver, passed down from her grandfather, was always by her side. When she landed a job at a top tech firm, Charli used her expertise to design innovative gadgets that changed the industry. Her colleagues marveled at her precision and creativity, often joking that she could build a spaceship with nothing but a screwdriver and a few scraps of metal. Charli's love affair with the humble screwdriver had taken her to incredible heights, proving that with the right tool and a bit of ingenuity, anything is possible.",
